   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Path Ride\n\nA line draws itself along a curve with the text riding behind its head, then the curve pulls taut and the text settles on a straight, centered baseline.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 3.2 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A tagline or a short phrase should travel across the frame before it settles, leading the eye from one side to the other.\n- You want text on a path, with each letter turned to the curve, and a clean readable line at the end.\n- The motion should follow a custom route: pass any SVG path in 1280×720 space.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The line should be an accent on its own, with no text riding it: use squiggle.\n- The text should loop around a closed ring: use ring-text.\n- The text should scroll in a straight strip: use infinite-marquee.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Follow the line\"\n- path (string): Path (1280×720), default \"M 120 560 C 360 120 560 120 640 360 S 920 600 1160 160\"\n- color (color): Text color, default \"#111111\"\n- line_color (color): Line color, default \"#fafafa\"\n- font_size (number, 16-120): Font size, default 44\n- font_weight (number, 100-900): Weight, default 700\n- line_width (number, 1-12): Line width, default 3\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
